  ["Product cost at 35 percent", "$14,000", "$14,000"],
  ["Service revenue after product cost", "$26,000", "$26,000"],
  ["Provider commission", "30 percent of gross\n= $12,000", "35 percent of revenue after product\n= $9,100"],
  ["Practice keeps before overhead", "$14,000 (35 percent)", "$16,900 (42 percent)"]
], [3360, 3000, 3000]));
c.push(P("Under the revenue based plan, the practice keeps thirty five percent of the service before a dollar reaches rent, the front desk, equipment, or owner pay, which on a busy month may not cover the cost of running the room. The margin protected plan keeps an additional twenty nine hundred dollars on the same production. On one provider, that is nearly thirty five thousand dollars a year.", { after: 100 }));
c.push(P("The provider does earn less on base commission in this illustration, because the original plan was overpaying relative to what the service could sustain. This is where the spiffs do their work. If the same injector prescribes four thousand dollars of homecare at a ten percent spiff and enrolls five members at fifty dollars each, that is six hundred fifty dollars more, and as retail and memberships grow, the provider has a clear path back to prior earnings and beyond, on revenue that is high margin for the practice.", { after: 60 }));

c.push(H2("Sample Plans by Seat"));
c.push(P("Use these as starting structures, then model them against your own numbers before you offer them.", { after: 100 }));
c.push(H3("New injector, building a book"));
["Base of $30 to $40 per hour, or the salary equivalent, for stability while the book fills.","Commission of 15 percent of service revenue after product cost, above a monthly production threshold.","Retail spiff of 10 percent on homecare prescribed.","Revisit the structure at ninety days and six months as production grows."].forEach(t => c.push(bullet(t)));
c.push(H3("Established injector, full book"));
["A modest base or draw, with a tiered commission on service revenue after product cost, for example 30 percent up to $50,000 and 35 percent above.","Retail spiff of 10 percent on homecare prescribed.","Membership spiff of $50 per new member enrolled."].forEach(t => c.push(bullet(t)));
c.push(H3("Aesthetician or laser technician, with a sample month"));
["Base of $22 to $28 per hour, plus 10 percent service commission and 10 to 15 percent retail commission."].forEach(t => c.push(bullet(t)));
