c.push(P("On the same production, the practice keeps roughly thirty thousand dollars more a year, and Maria has a clear path back to twelve thousand and beyond as she grows retail and memberships, on revenue that is profitable for the practice. Now you have the conversation. The script below is a model, in plain spoken language, that you make your own.", { after: 120 }));
c.push(quote("Maria, I want to talk through a change to how you\u2019re paid, and I want to be completely open with the numbers, because you\u2019ve earned that."));
c.push(quote("Right now you\u2019re producing about forty thousand a month, which is incredible. Here\u2019s what I\u2019ve realized though. The way the commission is set up, once I pay for the product we\u2019re using, the practice keeps barely enough to cover the room, the front desk, and everything it takes to keep your chair full. That\u2019s on me. I set it up that way, and it\u2019s not sustainable if I want to keep investing in you and in this place."));
c.push(quote("So here\u2019s what I\u2019m proposing, and I\u2019ve modeled it on your actual last three months. We move your commission to thirty five percent of your service revenue after the product cost, and we add a couple of things on top. You\u2019ll earn ten percent on every regimen you prescribe, and fifty dollars for every membership you bring in. Both of those are things you\u2019re already doing, you just haven\u2019t been paid for them."));
c.push(quote("When I run your real numbers through this, you land right around where you are now, and the moment you grow retail and memberships even a little, you\u2019re earning more than you ever have. And for the first time, the practice keeps enough to give you better equipment, better support, and a real future here."));
